Active [SimTalk] - Generator
Activates the object designated by <Path> (true) or deactivates it (false).
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Active:boolean
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyGenerator.Active := true
See also
Active [check box] - Generator
Active [SimTalk] - Generator
Plant Simulation Help 11-4399
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Duration [SimTalk] - Generator
Sets the time span between which the Generator designated by <Path> calls the Interval Control and the
Duration Control.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Duration:time
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type time.
Examples
MyGenerator.Duration.Type := "uniform"
MyGenerator.Duration.Start := 600 // from 10 minutes
MyGenerator.Duration.Stop := 1200 // to 20 minutes
Generator.Duration.setTypeAndAttr("cEmp", Table)
SimTalk
DurationCtrl [SimTalk]
See also
Duration [text box] - Generator
Duration Control [Generator]
Interval Control [Generator]
Duration [SimTalk] - Generator
11-4400 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

DurationCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>. Plant Simulation calls the Method after it
called the Interval Control of the Generator designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DurationCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
// does an entry exist?
if MyGenerator.DurationCtrl /= VOID // delete entry
   MyGenerator.DurationCtrl := VOID
end
See also
Duration Control [Generator]
DurationCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4401
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Interval [SimTalk] - Generator
Sets the time between two activations of the Interval Control of the Generator designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Interval:time
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type time.
Examples
obj.Interval.Type:= "Negexp"
obj.Interval.Beta:=150
obj.Interval.LowerBound:=1*60   // 1s *60
obj.Interval.UpperBound:= 10*60 // 10s *60
Generator.Interval.setTypeAndAttr("dEmp", Table)
SimTalk
IntervalCtrl [SimTalk]
See also
Interval [text box] - Generator
Interval Control [Generator]
Interval [SimTalk] - Generator
11-4402 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

IntervalCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>. Plant Simulation calls the Method during
the specified interval for the Generator designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.IntervalCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
// nothing entered yet?
if MyGenerator.IntervalCtrl = VOID 
   // enter reference to method
   MyGenerator.IntervalCtrl := &MyMethod
end
See also
Interval Control [Generator]
IntervalCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4403
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Start [SimTalk] - Generator
Sets the Start time of the Interval Control which the Generator designated by <Path> calls.
Remarks
The assignment has to be made during the Reset phase.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Start:time
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type time.
Examples
MyPlant.MyGenerator.Start.type := "const"
MyPlant.MyGenerator.Start := 120 // 2 minutes
Generator.Start.setTypeAndAttr("Normal", 30, 10)
See also
Start [text box] - Generator
Interval Control [Generator]
Start [SimTalk] - Generator
11-4404 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Stop [SimTalk] - Generator
Sets the Stop time of the Interval Control which the Generator designated by <Path> calls.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Stop:time
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type time.
Examples
// normally distributed end with left bound at 1 hour
// and open right bound
.InformationFlow.MyGenerator.Stop.Type := "normal"   // normal distribution
.InformationFlow.MyGenerator.Stop.Mu := 3600         // 1 hour
.InformationFlow.MyGenerator.Stop.Sigma := 600       // 10 minutes
.InformationFlow.MyGenerator.Stop.LowerBound := 1200 // 20 minutes
.InformationFlow.MyGenerator.Stop.UpperBound := 7200 // 2 hours
Generator.Stop.setTypeAndAttr("Normal", 1:00, 10)
See also
Stop [text box] - Generator
Interval Control [Generator]
AttributeExplorer
AttributeExplorer [object]
Use the object AttributeExplorer for managing the attributes defining the settings of the individual stations
in your simulation model at a single, central location.
Stop [SimTalk] - Generator
Plant Simulation Help 11-4405
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Image
Description
Instead of opening the dialog of each and every material flow object in your model and typing the
attribute values into the text boxes, you can define which attributes of which object the AttributeExplorer
gets and shows in a list window.
To do so, click Show Explorer. Then type in the different values, for the capacities, the times, etc., which
Plant Simulation writes back to the objects and uses in the model. You can Export this settings table as
a tab-delimited text file and Import this file into the AttributeExplorer of another simulation model, thus
using identical settings in several of your simulation models.
You can also show the attribute table of an AttributeExplorer in an HtmlReport, compare Display an
AttributeExplorer.
To show a tooltip with information about the AttributeExplorer, hover with the mouse over it.
To change the length of the graphic and the anchor points of the AttributeExplorer, click Show
Manipulators 
  on the Edit ribbon tab or press M on the keyboard.
Add the Object to the Simulation Model
To add the object AttributeExplorer to your simulation model, click 
  Manage Class Library > Basic
Objects > InformationFlow > AttributeExplorer on the Home ribbon tab.
Compare the sample models: Click the Window ribbon tab, click Start Page > Getting Started > Example
Models > Small Examples. Then, select the respective Category, the Topic, and the Example in the
dialog Examples Collection, and click Open Model.
